  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the following statements:<br />\r<br />\r(I)&nbsp;<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> is the least basic among hydroxides of lanthanides.<br />\r<br />\r(II) <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> and <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> possess almost the same ionic radii.<br />\r<br />\r(III) <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> can act as an oxidizing agent.<br />\r<br />\rWhich of the above is/are true?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "emPJb",
      "text": "<math> <mrow>  <mtext>(I)</mtext></mrow></math> and <math> <mrow>  <mtext>(III)</mtext></mrow></math>",
